  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A short, easy family walk of about an hour leads to a turquoise river and an impressive 42-metre waterfall, with a view of the surrounding cliffs. One of the most spectacular spots in the Var to admire with your dog after the walk.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access to the pool beneath the waterfall and swimming there are banned because of the risk of falling rocks (Dracénie tourist office, village of Sillans-la-Cascade). So this isn't a place to cool off with your dog, only a site to admire from the viewpoint (about 15 minutes' walk). Dogs must be kept on a leash and stay on the routes, as the site is a sensitive natural area listed under Natura 2000. The site was closed for development works from 27 October 2025 to 1 June 2026; check that it is open before you come. Parking is paid and compulsory from 1 April to 30 September (9am-7pm: 30 minutes free, then €1 every 15 minutes). The site can also be visited with a guided tour from the local saffron grower, Yannick Dolmetta, for those who want to extend the outing. A stop at the Chapelle Saint-Laurent is also possible before or after the walk.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come early or late in the day in summer, the site is very popular when it's hot.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Lac de Sainte-Croix is only about thirty minutes away, to extend the freshwater outing over the day.</p>
